merge_conflict_policy
  issue 991
  purpose "Remove the structural causes of merge conflicts so two branches touching unrelated work never collide."
  evidence "scripts/analyze-merge-conflicts.py ranks the paths that actually needed manual resolution across every merge commit in this repository."
  analysis "docs/case-studies/issue-991/merge-conflict-analysis.md"
  regenerate_all "bash scripts/regenerate-derived-artifacts.sh"
  verify "rust-script scripts/check-merge-conflict-policy.rs"
  invariant needs_no_local_git_config
    description "Every mechanism uses git's built-in union driver or a committed generator, so a fresh clone is already conflict-proof without running any git config command."
  invariant every_union_file_is_verified
    description "A union merge never blocks a merge, so each union-merged path must have a checker that fails when the unioned result is not canonical, unless the path declares union_is_terminal because every union of it is already correct."
  cause append_only_list
    description "A file whose whole body is one canonically ordered list of entries. Two branches appending adjacent entries conflict even though the entries are unrelated."
    mechanism union_merge_then_normalize
    resolution "git's built-in union driver keeps both inserted entries with no conflict; scripts/normalize-ordered-lists.rs restores the canonical order and removes duplicates."
    needs_git_config false
  cause mixed_list_and_code
    description "A list of entries that shares a file with real logic. The file cannot be union merged, because a union of two logic edits can compile and still be wrong."
    mechanism extract_list_then_union
    resolution "The list moves into a sibling file that contains nothing else; only that file is union merged."
    needs_git_config false
  cause derived_artifact
    description "A file produced from other committed sources by a generator. Any conflict in it is noise: the merged sources determine the correct content."
    mechanism union_merge_then_regenerate
    resolution "The union keeps the merge unblocked, the artifact's own verifier fails while the union result is stale, and scripts/regenerate-derived-artifacts.sh rebuilds it from the merged sources."
    needs_git_config false
  cause append_only_document
    description "A long prose document that every issue appends a new section to, so every branch edits the same end-of-file region."
    mechanism shard_per_issue
    resolution "Sections live one file per issue under a shard directory; the assembled document is a derived artifact."
    needs_git_config false
  cause sequential_file_name
    description "A new file claims the next free number in a sequence, so two branches independently create the same path and git reports an add/add conflict that no ordering can prevent."
    mechanism content_named_file
    resolution "New files are named after what they contain, so two branches produce two different names."
    needs_git_config false
  cause global_scalar_ratchet
    description "One shared constant records a repository-wide total, so every branch that changes any input rewrites the same line."
    mechanism shard_per_subject
    resolution "The budget is recorded per subject in its own file and summed; a branch only edits the shard it changed."
    needs_git_config false
  cause ci_workflow
    description "A CI workflow whose job body is one appended step per check. The steps are unordered with respect to each other, but YAML has no way to say so, so every branch that adds a check edits the same end-of-job region."
    mechanism shard_per_gate
    resolution "Each check becomes one file under a registry directory, named after the check; the workflow runs the registry once per stage and never names an individual check again, so adding a check stops editing the workflow at all."
    needs_git_config false
  cause automation_placeholder
    description "Branch-creation automation commits a placeholder whose body names the branch, so every branch carries a different body for the same path."
    mechanism union_merge_then_normalize
    resolution "The placeholder is union merged: keeping both provenance lines is the correct result and never conflicts."
    needs_git_config false
  artifact rust_declaration_lists
    cause append_only_list
    merge union
    list_kind rust_declarations
    normalize "rust-script scripts/normalize-ordered-lists.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/normalize-ordered-lists.rs"
    observed_conflicts 411
    note "Every body line is a mod declaration or a re-export block, so a union of two branches is always a superset of two correct files and the normalizer restores the canonical order."
    file
      path "src/lib.rs"
    file
      path "tests/unit/mod.rs"
      declares_directory "tests/unit"
    file
      path "tests/unit/specification/mod.rs"
      declares_directory "tests/unit/specification"
    file
      path "tests/integration/mod.rs"
      declares_directory "tests/integration"
    file
      path "tests/unit/ci-cd/mod.rs"
      note "No declares_directory: several entries are `#[path]` declarations that pull a `scripts/*.rs` gate into the test binary, so the canonical list is not the directory listing."
    file
      path "tests/source/mod.rs"
    file
      path "src/solver_handlers/modules.rs"
      extracted_from "src/solver_handlers/mod.rs"
      declares_directory "src/solver_handlers"
    file
      path "src/agentic_coding/modules.rs"
      extracted_from "src/agentic_coding/mod.rs"
      declares_directory "src/agentic_coding"
      note "Both runs moved out, not just the `mod` declarations: the re-export run is the longer of the two and every new capability appends to it, so leaving it behind would have kept the append point alive."
  artifact worker_module_list
    cause mixed_list_and_code
    merge union
    list_kind js_module_list
    normalize "rust-script scripts/normalize-ordered-lists.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/normalize-ordered-lists.rs"
    observed_conflicts 99
    file
      path "src/web/worker-modules.js"
      extracted_from "src/web/formal_ai_worker.js"
      declares_directory "src/web/worker"
      note "The list is exactly the sorted contents of the directory, so the normalizer regenerates it instead of merely reordering it."
  artifact seed_inventory
    cause mixed_list_and_code
    merge union
    normalize "rust-script scripts/generate-seed-registry.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/generate-seed-registry.rs"
    observed_conflicts 41
    note "One inventory serves both production paths. The Rust engine and the browser worker each used to carry their own copy of the seed file list, so adding a seed file meant appending to the same lines in two files -- and the two copies could drift apart about which files exist. The registry names every seed file once, with flags saying which consumer wants it, and both lists are generated from it."
    file
      path "data/meta/seed-registry.lino"
      extracted_from "src/seed/embedded.rs"
      declares_directory "data/seed"
      note "The generator ORs the flags of an entry a union left twice rather than taking the first, so a union that repeats a seed under two different flag sets keeps both branches' intent."
    file
      extracted_from "src/web/seed_loader.js"
  artifact seed_inventory_projections
    cause derived_artifact
    merge union
    regenerate "rust-script scripts/generate-seed-registry.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/generate-seed-registry.rs"
    path "src/seed/embedded_registry.rs"
    path "src/web/seed-files.js"
    note "`src/seed/embedded.rs` pulls its half in with `include!` rather than `mod`: rustfmt only reaches files a `mod` declaration names, so the generator owns every byte of the projection and a regeneration is byte-identical no matter which rustfmt version ran last."
  artifact branch_placeholder
    cause automation_placeholder
    merge union
    union_is_terminal true
    note "The file exists only to keep a directory tracked; its body is provenance. Any union of two provenance lines is already the correct content, so there is nothing left for a normalizer to do."
    file
      path ".gitkeep"
    observed_conflicts 44
  artifact seed_total_closure
    cause derived_artifact
    merge union
    path "data/seed/closure-generated-*.lino"
    regenerate "python3 scripts/close-total.py"
    verify "python3 scripts/audit-total-closure.py"
    observed_conflicts 261
  artifact self_ast_census
    cause derived_artifact
    merge union
    path "data/meta/self-ast/**"
    path "data/meta/self-ast.lino"
    note "The pattern is `**`, not `*.lino`: gitattributes globs follow gitignore rules, so a single star stops at a slash and left every nested shard -- data/meta/self-ast/src/lib.lino alone conflicted 29 times -- unprotected."
    regenerate "cargo run --example regenerate_self_ast_census"
    verify "cargo test --test unit issue_673_self_ast_census"
    observed_conflicts 145
  artifact seed_metadata_gaps
    cause derived_artifact
    merge union
    path "data/meta/seed-metadata-gaps-*.lino"
    regenerate "rust-script scripts/audit-seed-metadata.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/audit-seed-metadata.rs"
    observed_conflicts 75
  artifact hardcoded_language_allowlist
    cause derived_artifact
    merge union
    path "scripts/hardcoded-language-allowlist.txt"
    regenerate "rust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/check-hardcoded-language.rs"
    observed_conflicts 11
  artifact requirements_document
    cause append_only_document
    merge union
    path "REQUIREMENTS.md"
    shard_directory "docs/requirements"
    regenerate "rust-script scripts/assemble-requirements.rs --write"
    verify "rust-script scripts/assemble-requirements.rs"
    observed_conflicts 64
  artifact worker_modules
    cause sequential_file_name
    path "src/web/worker/formal_ai_worker_*.js"
    frozen_prefix_max 24
    note "formal_ai_worker_00 through formal_ai_worker_24 predate this policy and keep their numbers; every module added after issue 991 is named after its subject."
    observed_conflicts 11
  artifact worker_line_budget
    cause global_scalar_ratchet
    path "data/meta/worker-line-budget/*.lino"
    verify "rust-script scripts/check-worker-line-budget.rs"
    note "One shard per worker module replaces the single CEILING_TOTAL_LINES constant that every worker change used to rewrite."
  artifact ci_gate_registry
    cause ci_workflow
    verify "rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --check"
    observed_conflicts 35
    file
      path "data/meta/ci-gates/*.lino"
      extracted_from ".github/workflows/release.yml"
      declares_directory "data/meta/ci-gates"
      note "The shards are deliberately not union merged: two branches adding a gate write two differently named files, so there is nothing to union. The verify command is what keeps the extraction from unwinding -- it fails when the lint job runs a gate command inline again."
  deferred shared_logic_edits
    reason "Two branches changing the same behaviour in the same function is a genuine semantic collision: a human has to decide which change wins, and no file layout can decide it for them. Mechanizing it would be lying. The mitigations are indirect -- keep files small (the file-size gates), keep one subject per file, and move every embedded *list* out into its own union-merged file, which is what the artifacts above do. Each path below is ranked mostly by list churn that has already been extracted, so the residual count overstates the irreducible part."
    path "src/seed.rs"
    path "src/solver.rs"
    path "src/solver_dispatch.rs"
    path "src/main.rs"
    path "src/web/app.js"
    path "src/agentic_coding/planner.rs"
    path "tests/unit/formal_ai.rs"
    path "tests/e2e/tests/multilingual.spec.js"
    path "tests/e2e/playwright.local.config.js"
  deferred curated_seed_records
    reason "A seed file is a curated body of knowledge, not an append-only list: entries are grouped by subject and later entries reference earlier ones, so a union merge can produce a bundle that parses and still means something nobody wrote. New knowledge belongs in a new subject-named seed file, which is why `data/seed/` has grown to one file per subject; these two predate that convention and are split subject-by-subject as they are touched."
    path "data/seed/roles.lino"
    path "data/seed/multilingual-responses.lino"
  deferred lockfile_and_manifest
    reason "Cargo.toml's version line and Cargo.lock's matching entry are owned by release automation, so every branch that outlives one release rewrites them. Union merging a lockfile produces a file cargo rejects. The resolution is mechanical and already scripted -- take main's version, rerun `cargo update -p formal-ai` -- but it is a resolution, not an avoidance."
    path "Cargo.toml"
    path "Cargo.lock"
  deferred recorded_transcript
    reason "A captured Agent CLI session is evidence: its bytes are what the tool actually emitted. Re-recording it on both sides of a merge produces two different valid transcripts and a human must pick one. New captures go to new content-named files; this one is ranked only because it was re-recorded repeatedly before that rule existed."
    path "docs/case-studies/issue-538/agent-cli-session-self-ast.json"
  deferred long_form_documents
    reason "README.md and ARCHITECTURE.md are read top-to-bottom by humans, so unlike REQUIREMENTS.md their section order carries meaning that a per-issue shard directory would destroy. Sharding them is tracked separately; until a shard order can be expressed without flattening the narrative, the mitigation is that new material goes to a topic page under docs/ and these two only gain a link."
    path "README.md"
    path "ARCHITECTURE.md"
